WEBVTT

NOTE Draft machine transcription; human accuracy and sound review pending.
Buncrana spelling confirmed by the site owner.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
It's saying to the man in Buncrana
that I met a few years back.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.540
He left Buncrana in the 1950s
with £15.

3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.940
His family worked really hard to bring
together £15 for him to emigrate.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.980
Six weeks after he emigrated,
he didn't get work in London.

5
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.860
He had £5 left, and there's a very
successful businessman today.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.320
He had £5 left in his pocket.

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.740
He put it in an envelope.
He wrote a letter home

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.440
and said to his parents
how well he was doing.

9
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.740
So there's stories, there's memories,
there's impact.

10
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.300
People matter.

11
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.500
You matter.

12
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.500
The people that you work with,

13
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.800
the people that's in your family,
in your communities,

14
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.900
everybody matters.

15
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.360
And there's a real, real opportunity
in this book to call that out.

